{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system","id":1071339,"title":"[1E] Hacking the System","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-31T11:28:02-07:00","id":1071339,"title":"[1E] Hacking the System","content":"Ever notice how Time mages only have 5 or 6 spells they regularly cast? Or how Mind mages spam spells left and right? Or how Spirit doesn't do -anything- after you've yelled at your player for trying to Rouse every doorknob and tennis shoe?<br /> <br /> I made a couple of fairly large changes to my 1E game that have played pretty well that I thought I'd share. Some of you may hate the ideas (and I'm okay with that), some of you might not. The problem stems from the developer's love of Mind spells and the wholly arbitrary nature of Spell Aspect. So how to address that? Change Spell Aspect at the meta level than per Spell:<br /> <br /> <b>1. Spell Aspect</b><br /> Covert - Compelling (*), Knowing (*), Unveiling (*), Ruling (**), Veiling (**), and Shielding (**)<br /> Vulgar (-1 dice) - Fraying (***), Perfecting (***), Weaving (***)<br /> Vulgar - Patterning (****), Uraveling (*****)<br /> Vulgar (+1 dice) - Making (*****), Unmaking (*****)<br /> <br /> Now instead of an arbitrary system, we have one that's fair for every Arcana. Bonus? Easy as heck to remember. It's also easy to 'tweak' the settings to your own liking for Paradox by just adjusting the 'dox impact at the meta level. Too much 'dox? Make * - *** Covert and **** and ***** Vulgar.<br /> <br /> Now, the big difference (at my setting) is multiple Vulgars in-Scene accumulation. Right now we play at every <i>third</i> Vulgar spell adds +1 instead of every Vulgar. Again, tweak to your liking.<br /> <br /> What we end up with is a system that lets every Arcana participate without the arbitrary shackles and love/hate of the devs, with <b>two easy 'switches' to adjust the <i>overall </i>Paradox</b> in the game. This is more a demonstration of how the system at large <i>can </i>be addressed to give every Arcana equal opportunity.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Spread the Love</b><br /> The second major change was to take all of the trait (Skill, Att) boosting spells from <b>Mind </b>and divide them: <b>Mind </b>affects <b>Mental </b>traits, and a duplicate spell for <b>Spirit </b>affects the <b>Social </b>traits. This gives Spirit a bit more utility and makes it harder to lean on boosting rather than XP spends for Mind mages. For those concerned with 'thematics', Social traits are used heavily to deal with Spirits, so it makes sense Spirit mages would have found a way to boost them. Social traits aren't <i>wholly </i>mental, either, and classifying things like charisma and presence under Spirit makes just as much <i>logical sense</i> as classifying them under Mind. Mind players will scream in anguish, Spirit players will randomly hug you and gift you with baked goods.<br /> <br /> Again, these changes might not be to everyone's liking and everyone's game is different. They've worked well for mine so I thought I'd share for those still on 1E. For the super nerdy, I've got a SQL table full of every spell that I used to make some handy graphs showing the disparity in Arcana by RAW and why changes might be warranted:<br /> <br /> Below you can see that Mind has an average of <b>twice as many spells</b> as any other Arcana, and <b>two to three times as many Covert</b> spells. Level the playing field, yo.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://imgur.com/R4AF0XD.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","user":"grey_goose","date":". 03-31-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T13:09:53-07:00","id":1071389,"title":"","content":"Not really necessary now that 2e is out, but I'm glad it's working for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:28:48-07:00","id":1071443,"title":"","content":"Well 2E <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024148-status-and-resources?p=1026733#post1026733\">doesn't work for me / wasn't designed for large scale games</a>, so I'm rolling with 1E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","user":"grey_goose","date":". 03-31-2017, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:00:59-07:00","id":1071464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system#post1071339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or how Spirit doesn't do -anything- after you've yelled at your player for trying to Rouse every doorknob and tennis shoe?</div> </div> </div> </div>So now it just does social boosting? Do you have advice for these storytellers who don't let the Spirit arcana work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:13:04-07:00","id":1071475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1071464#post1071464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now it just does social boosting? Do you have advice for these storytellers who don't let the Spirit arcana work?</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Gosh no, it does everything it did before -plus- social boosting. It was more a nod to the situations where Spirit players want to talk to <i>anything </i>that might have a Spirit and bog play down <i>because they can't do anything else</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T06:22:31-07:00","id":1071696,"title":"","content":"Spirit can do almost anything...I don't understand how a Mage with Spirit would be stuck just talking to spirits when you can also command them, or pact with them, or make them into a familiar, or completely reshape them at the higher end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T06:48:05-07:00","id":1071702,"title":"","content":"Just rouse ambient spirits of &quot;not being awkward in social situation&quot; and order them to aid you. No need for special rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T18:00:58-07:00","id":1075655,"title":"","content":"The spirit thing makes sense. Spirit mages are all about talking to things and RAW the only way 1e Spirit supports that is by enslaving them or becoming a Adept of Prime so you can directly bribe them. At least with the social boosting magic you can enhance your ability to negotiate with them. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1071696#post1071696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit can do almost anything...I don't understand how a Mage with Spirit would be stuck just talking to spirits when you can also command them, or pact with them, or make them into a familiar, or completely reshape them at the higher end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you should have to wait until Mastery to have fun with any arcana. All the other arcana lets you do stuff spontaneously, so it's notable to me that so much of 1e Spirit requires you to go off and make deals with people that other people can't interact with to get use out of it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1071702#post1071702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just rouse ambient spirits of &quot;not being awkward in social situation&quot; and order them to aid you. No need for special rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds easy right? But if there's <i>always </i>a spirit of whatever you need on hand in the shadow minding it's own business that you can easily hijack to work it's magic through, then Spirit become weighted to the other end of the power curve.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T18:27:56-07:00","id":1075661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1071696#post1071696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit can do almost anything...I don't understand how a Mage with Spirit would be stuck just talking to spirits when you can also command them, or pact with them, or make them into a familiar, or completely reshape them at the higher end.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're coming at it from the wrong angle- the issue is that Spirit tricks require more active engagement and creativity from the ST at the table, compared to a spell that just accomplishes whatever effect with just the player stating their intent and a single roll. IE, Spirit spells in practice involve lots of mother-may-i about &quot;is there a fire spirit here? what numina does the spirit have?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:10:49-07:00","id":1075693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1075661#post1075661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're coming at it from the wrong angle- the issue is that Spirit tricks require more active engagement and creativity from the ST at the table, compared to a spell that just accomplishes whatever effect with just the player stating their intent and a single roll. IE, Spirit spells in practice involve lots of mother-may-i about &quot;is there a fire spirit here? what numina does the spirit have?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically any creative application of an arcana that doesn't involve something directly based on published material requires an equal level of engagement and creativity from an ST. You can't get around that. Spirit might suffer more from that than other arcana, but it still doesn't mean that Spirit can't accomplish almost anything, and it also doesn't mean that Spirit is relegated to just knocking on random objects and asking if anyone is home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:56:18-07:00","id":1075777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1075655#post1075655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds easy right? But if there's <i>always </i>a spirit of whatever you need on hand in the shadow minding it's own business that you can easily hijack to work it's magic through, then Spirit become weighted to the other end of the power curve.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have two dots in Presence or one in Socialize the Spirit is in you, extremely weak and dormant. But ready to be fed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T02:48:05-07:00","id":1075811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1075777#post1075777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have two dots in Presence or one in Socialize the Spirit is in you, extremely weak and dormant. But ready to be fed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're confusing spirits and goetia, you don't keep spirits inside yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T03:05:56-07:00","id":1075815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1075811#post1075811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're confusing spirits and goetia, you don't keep spirits inside yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not. Look at the Coaxing the Spirits (Spirit 1), I know that is from 2E but it might help to understand it. I lets you induce responses in animals by affecting spirits 'inside' of them. While humans don't have spirits of their own they are generating them. Killing produces vicious spirits with murderous intent, opera house has potent spirits of singing. 'Not being awkward in social situation' also produces such spirts albeit extreamly weak. They lay dormant, more like a grass or fungus, but if you know where to look you can feed them and control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T03:44:45-07:00","id":1075825,"title":"","content":"They'd be Motes at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T03:55:19-07:00","id":1075830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1075825#post1075825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd be Motes at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. But they are there, waiting to be abused <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Whole spell is based on Motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T06:13:02-07:00","id":1075852,"title":"","content":"OP is pretty explicit about this being a 1e only hack though. In 1e coaxing the spirit just improved an object's equipment bonus for an action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T06:24:24-07:00","id":1075856,"title":"","content":"Nothing stops OP from using version of Coaxing the Spirits in 1E. I just think it makes more sense to wake dormant spirits than just flat out add Social modifiers to a Spirit arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T07:55:21-07:00","id":1075881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1075856#post1075856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing stops OP from using version of Coaxing the Spirits in 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than their explicitly expressed desire to keep using 1e, right? When someone says &quot;Hey 2e doesn't suit my tastes, I prefer using 1e because reasons&quot;, people replying with &quot;use this thing from 2e&quot; doesn't seem very helpful to me?<br /> <br /> RAW 1e Spirit is about interacting with spirits. Moving social dice adders into it expands it to interaction in general. Warlocks don't really loose anything, since Mind probably still has the actual mental manipulation powers in it, like emotional urging, telepathy, implanting thoughts, mind control, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:07:39-07:00","id":1075890,"title":"","content":"Wut? Hack is a hack no matter where it comes from. Be it some guy sitting in his shack in London, other gameline or second edition of your game even if you don't like it as a whole.<br /> <br /> Adding social modifiers to Spirit is nothing new, it was a hack a long time ago and didn't like at the time I played 1E. The thing is that I don't care about the mentioned spell. I'm just talking about setting assumptions that can change/repair/broaden the Spirit arcanum. Motes are everywhere, they are a plankton of the Shadow. Weak but coaxable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:12:33-07:00","id":1075894,"title":"","content":"Teah but motes can't <i>do</i> anything. The spirits in 2e Coaxing aren't motes, they're just spirits that aren't awake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:22:41-07:00","id":1075903,"title":"","content":"As I've said earlier you need to feed them, streanghten. Applying bonus to action is a 3rd dot in 2E and I don't recomend to be able pull that trick on lower dots. But it's doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:38:07-07:00","id":1075909,"title":"","content":"So your response to &quot;this hack lets spirit mages be a little more spontaneous with what they can do in play&quot; is &quot;make spirit mages play gardener/baby sitters for baby spirits until they grow to a point where they have something useful to contribute to their pokemon trainer&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:45:35-07:00","id":1075912,"title":"","content":"Heh, dude/dudess. I'm giving a possibility for streghtening Motes. You can do it hand feeding them and changing their clothes or by casting a spell, like normal mages do. <br /> <br /> Ow, it's a cute little Mote! -&gt; 'Boost a spirit' spell or watheva -&gt; 'Order the spirit to boost you' spell.<br /> I belive that at 4th dot you can cast as a single effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T09:54:39-07:00","id":1075932,"title":"","content":"So how does that help someone who isn't an adept/master and who can't reformat any random spirit into whatever is handy at the moment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:03:50-07:00","id":1075969,"title":"","content":"...<br /> Those are literally two turns of casting spells. First bolster, then command. If you are an adept you can do it in a single swipe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:15:00-07:00","id":1075976,"title":"","content":"in <i>1e</i>, the only spell that does what you suggest is Spirit 5 - Shape Spirit. So what exactly is a mage who's got 1e Spirit 1-4 supposed to do on the fly with the arcana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:50:10-07:00","id":1076007,"title":"","content":"Use Creative Thaumaturgy, port Control Ghost and Quicken Corpse to work with Spirits. In 1E Coaxing the Spirit grants flat +1 dice but it's still a 1 dot effect, I imagine that you could grant more dice on 3rd dot, coax your bow tie or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:07:03-07:00","id":1076020,"title":"","content":"... How is that <i>any different</i> than a Spirit version of Augment the Mind that enhances Social abilities, or a Spirit Gain Skill that enhances social skills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:27:20-07:00","id":1076043,"title":"","content":"Principle. And requirements. Also you don't need to hack anything, just use Creative Thaum. If you don't have 'a neat bow tie of a politician +5' (its not a Mote) or someone destroyed/banned all spirits in your vicinity or you are in the astral you can't boost spirits from obvious reasons.<br /> But if you are fine with adding Social Interactions to the Arcanum Purview I can't help more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Purview</b>: Exorcism, the Shadow<br /> Realm, soul retrieval, spirits, the<br /> Gauntlet </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:44:22-07:00","id":1076081,"title":"","content":"While the principle is sound I don't think I'd allow a mote of &quot;not being socially awkward&quot; to be just floating around a person at any given time. Emotional spirits aren't common, and even when they are there they're more likely to be anchored to something other than a person. In the Book of Spirits there's a mote of happiness but it doesn't follow around the girl that generated it, instead it stays in her room where her happiness is generated and waits for her to come home to prey on her. I would use Coaxing the Spirit from 1e to give an equipment bonus to a piece of equipment the Mage is using to try to not be socially awkward. For instance showing up with a bottle of wine that's been boosted with Coaxing the Spirit to make a good impression at a house party. You can generate essentially the same effect, but have to put more thought into your props. I'd run it that way for 2e as well.<br /> <br /> I still disagree with OP that Spirit is only good for talking to spirits, even in 1e that's clearly not the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:45:54-07:00","id":1076182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1076081#post1076081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still disagree with OP that Spirit is only good for talking to spirits, even in 1e that's clearly not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I never said that. I referred to <i>situations</i>, not the Arcana at large. If you want to disagree, you're disagreeing with your own mis-reading and not me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1076043#post1076043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you are fine with adding Social Interactions to the Arcanum Purview I can't help more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. And if you are fine with:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>The mage can whisper to a spirit sleeping within a material object and ask for its aid, <b>making it easier to use the object</b>.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Being defined as 'i can haz bonus on people from bowtie and ignores RAW spell' then I can't help more... but don't quote RAW when it suits you and completely ignore it elsewhere. That's just <i>silly</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T00:40:44-07:00","id":1076355,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3557\" data-vbnamecard=\"3557\">grey_goose</a> Tell me. Do you only use printed spells? Remember that Creative Thaumataurgy is a part of the rules(a lot harder in 1E then in 2E, I agree) and I'm telling you to craft spells that suit your needs while making them stay under the Arcanum purview. RAW tell you to use them As Intended.<br /> Adding Social to Spirit is like adding Physical to Forces. Theres no need to make those Purviews incoherent when you can achieve results without altering them. Spirit uses spirits and spirit related phenomena to achieve it's goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T01:02:11-07:00","id":1076362,"title":"","content":"I just used <i>your</i> example. Citing a spell and then saying 'Oh, but CT' is just moving the goal posts. Clearly anything is possible with CT in a lax enough environment, and I'm comfortable in saying that you're used to playing in a much more permissive environment than I am. If you play games where Adepts and Masters are a dime a dozen and every conceivable Spirit is in earshot waiting to toss your salad, have at it. I don't, for various reasons, much like I don't move goal posts in discussions.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if I wanted to play a game that was basically nothing but rationalization (collapsing them probability waves, yo, I can do ANYTHING), I would play Ascension or just write free-form fiction.<br /> <br /> (I figure as long as you're bringing 2E discussion into a clearly 1E thread, we might as well just talk about any game line or style.)<br /> <br /> Honestly? I find 'debating' the scope of Spirits in Monty Haul games <i>boring</i>. It was played out 10 years ago on the original forums. If that's what gets you off, enjoy <b>your </b>game by all means. Just don't suggest that interpretation is RAW by claiming 'CT' when your attempt to wield RAW falls flat. If anything is 'incoherent', that type of discussion is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","user":"grey_goose","date":". 04-11-2017, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T01:42:06-07:00","id":1076369,"title":"","content":"You're right, it seems incoherent on my side but it's hard to talk about rules considering only written spells when you can and should create new ones to help your character and game.<br /> <br /> I've never played Mage but in last chronicle my players had max 3 dots in an arcanum and were considered 'talented and well above average'. I have used only one Adept npc throughout the 5 months play. And I'm not saying that all spirits are everywhere but I'm saying that if you have some Socialize on your sheet you have motes of it on you. With a little effort you can bring it up to your aid. If you didn't talk to people in two days the motes can be dead and won't help you but in this situation cast a spell that speeds up a buildup of spirits when you generate the proper resonance. <br /> <br /> I'm talking about hacks just like you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T06:47:29-07:00","id":1076450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1076369#post1076369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, it seems incoherent on my side but it's hard to talk about rules considering only written spells when you can and should create new ones to help your character and game.</div> </div> </div> </div>...if you know what you're doing.<br /> <br /> For example, you suggest 'porting' <i>Control Ghost</i> and<i> Quicken Corpse</i> over to Spirit.<br /> - <i>Control Spirit</i> already exists as the analog to <i>Control Ghost</i>.<br /> - <i>Rouse Spirit</i> already exists at the analog to <i>Quicken Corpse</i> <b>and </b><br /> - <i>Shape Spirit</i> <b>unequivocally </b>dictates 'improving' a Spirit instantly by spell is a Mastery feat. Any 'CT' suggesting you can instantly alter a Spirit otherwise isn't 'CT', <b>it's blatantly ignoring the rules.</b><br /> <br /> To be perfectly blunt, I find your (lack of) understanding of CT and the body of RAW spells to be incoherent and impossible to take seriously as any sort of 'solution'. <b>Yes</b>, CT is a viable option, but it's not to be used to <i>bypass RAW</i> which is clearly how you use it.<br /> <br /> If you want to start a thread about <b>your </b>'<b>hacks</b>'; i.e. letting CT expand the purview of Spirit (to what I consider incoherent) feel free, but please don't use your hacks as an argument to mine. <i>At the very least</i>, they only address <b>half</b> of my intent -- the other being to remove a bit of the glaring over-utility of Mind. I've played and run Mage 1E for ten years now, at times for <i>dozens </i>of characters. I'm quite content that<i> my</i> hacks address the issues that<i> I have</i> in <i>my </i>game and the purpose of the thread was to share them with <i>others who might have similar issues</i> in <i>their </i>game(s). At no point did I ever suggest they were changes everyone should adopt. <br /> <br /> To be honest? I mostly made the thread to talk about the arbitrary Aspect 'system', not have the same old tired 'Spirit zoMG' debate. If you want that, go start your very own '<i>Spirit Can Do Anything (With CT)!</i>' thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:04:31-07:00","id":1076459,"title":"","content":"But your suggestion is skipping steps that make it more complex than you use as an example. There aren't actually any Socialize or Persuasion Spirits, there's Lust and Fear and Hunger Spirits. And if you are surrounded by motes based on your behavior, those motes are gonna come in multiple different flavors. So the mage would have to go through these steps if they wanted to do it spontaneously.<br /> Cast a spell to see across the gauntlet<br /> Cast a spell like Know Spirit to scan a mote to see if it's the right type of mote to enhance, keep casting while you scan the spirit plankton around you until you find something suitable<br /> Cast a spell to pull the mote across the gauntlet<br /> Cast a spell to anchor it to you so it doesn't fall into slumber, because it has no numina and no essence<br /> Cast a spell to feed it mana so it has essence so it can do stuff like manifest out of twilight<br /> Cast a spell that buffs the mote's stats so it can do stuff<br /> Cast a spell that compels the mote to do what you want<br /> <br /> That's <i>complicated.</i> Some of those spell effects are Canon spells ranging from 2-4 dots, so it's hardly a 2 spell solution like you suggest.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T12:27:35-07:00","id":1076626,"title":"","content":"I'm not clear on why you picked Spirit to get the social enhancements. Why didn't you pick Space? It has even fewer spells according to your chart. You could phrase it as the manipulations of sympathies, already in the purview of Space.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, didn't notice the guy was banned. Guess I won't get an answer for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-11-2017, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T15:06:14-07:00","id":1076673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1076626#post1076626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not clear on why you picked Spirit to get the social enhancements. Why didn't you pick Space? It has even fewer spells according to your chart. You could phrase it as the manipulations of sympathies, already in the purview of Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>OP explained it in their opening post, but remember that in 1e sympathetic connections didn't have any effects on their subjects like they do in 2e. 1e Space was all about moving things from point a to point b, or blocking things from moving from point a to point b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T15:54:14-07:00","id":1076685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1076673#post1076673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP explained it in their opening post, but remember that in 1e sympathetic connections didn't have any effects on their subjects like they do in 2e. 1e Space was all about moving things from point a to point b, or blocking things from moving from point a to point b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually true, it was always in the fluff that Sympathy did more than act as a regulator on that stuff, it was just completely ignored in the mechanics because none of the writers liked doing space spells for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:17:29-07:00","id":1077015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071339-1e-hacking-the-system?p=1076459#post1076459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But your suggestion is skipping steps that make it more complex than you use as an example. There aren't actually any Socialize or Persuasion Spirits, there's Lust and Fear and Hunger Spirits. And if you are surrounded by motes based on your behavior, those motes are gonna come in multiple different flavors. So the mage would have to go through these steps if they wanted to do it spontaneously.<br /> Cast a spell to see across the gauntlet<br /> Cast a spell like Know Spirit to scan a mote to see if it's the right type of mote to enhance, keep casting while you scan the spirit plankton around you until you find something suitable<br /> Cast a spell to pull the mote across the gauntlet<br /> Cast a spell to anchor it to you so it doesn't fall into slumber, because it has no numina and no essence<br /> Cast a spell to feed it mana so it has essence so it can do stuff like manifest out of twilight<br /> Cast a spell that buffs the mote's stats so it can do stuff<br /> Cast a spell that compels the mote to do what you want<br /> <br /> That's <i>complicated.</i> Some of those spell effects are Canon spells ranging from 2-4 dots, so it's hardly a 2 spell solution like you suggest.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I still think that there is less steps than you count here but before I say how many we must answer the question where are the motes and rank 1 spirits. Coaxing lets you target material item and compel its ghost to influence it. Where this spirit is? Twilight or Shadow? If in Shadow how can you affect it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}